// thousand_spheres_two_pillars_slitpass_TEST_100floaters_res2x_gas.prm
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ISOLATION TEST (4 of 4): RESOLUTION doubled relative to TEST_100floaters_gas.prm
// (domain <160,75,180> -> <320,150,180>, X doubled, Y rescaled to 150 to satisfy
// Utility.h's bed-consistency assertion, Z untouched -- same pattern as the
// original 128->160 widening). Sphere radius kept LITERALLY at 1.0 LU
// (unchanged) -- Pass-3 OFF (matching TEST_100floaters' crashing baseline
// exactly, for a clean apples-to-apples comparison).
//
// IMPORTANT NUANCE: in this framework 1 LU is always exactly 1 lattice cell, so
// a radius=1.0 sphere is ALWAYS 2 cells across, regardless of domain cell count
// -- doubling domainSize[0] does NOT change how many cells resolve this
// particular sphere. What it DOES change: scalingFactor (derived from
// domainSize[0]) doubles, so avgParticleDiameter/liquidHeight/floorHeight (all
// derived from it) also double -- avgParticleDiameter=20.00485,
// liquidHeight=57.254, floorHeight=82.788, surface Z=140.04. This tests whether
// resolving the AMBIENT physics (bed-particle scale, water depth) more finely
// changes the outcome for the same literal radius=1.0 spheres -- a different
// question from TEST_100floaters_r2/r3's "make the sphere itself bigger" tests.
//
// 100 spheres: one layer at Z=145 (above the new Z~140.04 surface), 10x10 grid,
// X=[20,200], Y=[10,140] (both 2x the original footprint, matching the domain
// scale). Pillars scaled 2x to center (276,38,90)/(276,112,90), radius
// unchanged at 8.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1000 SMALL SPHERES, ALL densityRatio=0.5, DYNAMICALLY-COMPUTED (non-overridden)
// GRAVITY, all starting OUTSIDE/ABOVE water, dropped in 10 layers of 100 (one
// layer released every 1000 timesteps) upstream of two cylinder pillars pushed
// to the far downstream (right) end of a WIDENED domain, testing whether they
// pass cleanly through the three slits (pillar-wall / inter-pillar / pillar-
// wall) instead of clogging.
//
// v1 -> v2 changes, and why:
//   - v1 released all 1000 spheres simultaneously at settlingSteps=300 (they
//     straddled the free surface). That caused a fatal NaN-quaternion crash at
//     step 321 (job 4056593) -- a real, previously-characterized instability
//     from releasing many bodies at once (same root cause as this session's dry
//     DEM validation work: runRotatingDrum's all-at-once release showed the same
//     kind of energy spike that runPacking's one-at-a-time protocol never did).
//   - Fix: ALL spheres now start well ABOVE the free surface (dry, in air, no
//     initial fluid interaction at all), arranged in 10 Z-layers of 100 spheres
//     each. Each layer's settlingSteps is offset by 1000 from the previous one
//     (300, 1300, 2300, ..., 9300) -- lowest layer (closest to the water) drops
//     first, staggering the total release into 10 events of 100 bodies instead
//     of one event of 1000.
//   - Domain widened in X (128->160). Y CANNOT be widened independently of X:
//     Utility.h's getAvgDiameterScalingFactor derives scalingFactor purely from
//     domainSize[0] (scalingFactor = domainSize[0] / (generationDomainSize_SI[0]
//     * bedCopiesInX)), then asserts domainSize[1] == scalingFactor *
//     generationDomainSize_SI[1] * bedCopiesInY EXACTLY -- an initial v2 attempt
//     using Y=90 (a different widening ratio than X's 1.25x) failed this
//     assertion immediately (job 4056668, <1s into the run: "Generated bed with
//     copies and simulation domain do not match!", expected 75 got 90). Fixed
//     by using Y=75 (the SAME 1.25x ratio as X: 60*1.25=75), cellsPerBlock Y
//     25 (3*25=75, block COUNT unchanged at 4x3x6=72, still one node/72
//     processes). This constraint applies even though useParticleBed=false
//     here (no bed is actually loaded) -- the check runs unconditionally.
//     Z (height) untouched, so the free-surface derivation below still holds.
//
// Free surface -- v3 -> v4 fix: avgParticleDiameter/liquidHeight/floorHeight are
// NOT fixed constants, they're DERIVED from domainSize[0] via Utility.h's
// scalingFactor = domainSize[0] / (generationDomainSize_SI[0] * bedCopiesInX).
// v3 reused the reference run's numbers (avgParticleDiameter=8.00194, surface
// Z=56.02) verbatim, but that reference used domainSize[0]=128, not this file's
// widened 160 -- a 1.25x mismatch that silently shifted the REAL surface up to
// Z~70, so v3's "above water" Z=60..87 layers actually started AT/NEAR the true
// waterline. Result: catastrophic MEM force blowup (forceZ up to 1e+26, garbage)
// within 17 steps of the first layer's release (job 4056761, step 317) ->
// heap corruption -> SIGABRT. Rescaled correctly here for THIS file's actual
// domainSize[0]=160: avgParticleDiameter = 8.00194*(160/128) = 10.0024,
// liquidHeight = 10.0024*2.862 = 28.63, floorHeight = 10.0024*4.1393 = 41.41,
// surface Z = floorHeight+liquidHeight = 70.03. All 10 sphere layers (Z=76..103)
// now sit comfortably above that (previously Z=60..87, against the wrong 56.02).
//
// Pillars (in the corrected Y=75 domain, radius unchanged at 8, moved further
// right into the wider X=160 domain -- unaffected by the surface-height fix,
// CylinderPillars span the full Z=0..180 regardless):
//   Pillar 1: center (138, 19, 90), r=8  -> occupies Y=11..27, wall gap 11 LU
//   Pillar 2: center (138, 56, 90), r=8  -> occupies Y=48..64, wall gap 11 LU
//   Inter-pillar gap: 21 LU (Y=27..48)
// Sphere diameter 2.0 -- 5.5x+ margin on the tightest (11 LU) gap.
//
// 1000 spheres: 10 layers (Z=76,79,...,103) x 10x10 X-Y grid per layer,
// X=[10,100] (well upstream/left of the X=138 pillars), Y=[5,70] (spans all
// three lanes within the corrected Y=75 domain, clear of both walls). Grid
// spacing (9.0 X, 6.5 Y, 3.0 Z-layer) all comfortably exceed the 2.0 sphere
// diameter -- no overlap at spawn.
//
// PhysicsParameters: NO gravityOverride -- dynamically computed gravity.
//
// Domain: <160, 75, 180> / cellsPerBlock <40, 25, 30> = 4x3x6 = 72 processes
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

BlockForestParameters
{
   cellsPerBlock                 < 80, 50, 30 >;
   periodicity                   < 1, 0, 0 >;
   loadSnapshot                  false;
   storeSnapshot                 true;
   snapshotFrequency             10000;
   snapshotBaseFolder            snapshots;
}

DomainParameters
{
   domainSize         <320, 150, 180>;
   wavePeriods        1;
   liquidHeightFactor 2.862;
   floorHeightFactor  4.1393;
   initialAmplitude   0;
}

PIDParameters
{
   targetMeanVelocityMagnitude 0.02;
   proportionalGain            2e-4;
   derivativeGain              1e-6;
   integralGain                2e-4;
   maxRamp                     1e-4;
   minActuatingVariable        0;
   maxActuatingVariable        1e-3;
}

PhysicsParameters
{
   enableWetting     false;
   timesteps         10000;
   Re                3100;
   Fr                1.31;
   We                15.6188;
   useHardcodedUnits true;
   // no gravityOverride -- dynamically computed gravity, per request
}

ParticleParameters
{
   inFileName spheres_out.dat;
   bedCopiesInX 1;
   bedCopiesInY 1;
   densityRatio 2.55;
   fixingHeightFactor 1.5;
   frictionCoefficient 0.5;
   restitutionCoefficient 0.97;
   numSubCycles 10;
   useLubricationCorrection true;
   useNoSlipParticles false;
   useParticleBed false;
}

CylinderPillars
{
   CylinderPillar
   {
      center < 276, 38, 90 >;
      radius 8;
   }
   CylinderPillar
   {
      center < 276, 112, 90 >;
      radius 8;
   }
}

